# Project Architecture

Personal portfolio site for Rohit Gupta, deployed as a static GitHub Pages repo (`rohit-gh.github.io`).

## Stack

- Plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript — no build step, bundler, or `package.json`
- **UIkit 3.25.16** (jsDelivr) on all active pages
- **custom.css** — shared design system for `index.html` and `legal.html`
- Assets are committed directly; no image pipeline or CMS
- jQuery removed; use UIkit data attributes (`uk-*`) and vanilla JS only

## File Roles

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `index.html` | Main landing page — persona cards, hero, navigation |
| `legal.html` | Terms of Use, Privacy Policy, and Disclaimer |
| `old.html` | Legacy Bootstrap layout — reference only, do not extend |
| `custom.css` | Shared styles for all active pages (tokens, layout, cards, footer, legal) |
| `rohit-*.webp` | Persona card images (developer, traveller, blogger) |
| `rohit-gupta.vcf` | Contact card download |
| `favicon.ico` | Local favicon (all pages) |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | Release and redesign history |

## Page Framework

All active pages share the same shell:

- `body.site-shell` — flex column, full viewport height
- `header.site-header` — navbar + offcanvas nav
- `main.site-main` — page content inside `.site-container`
- `footer.footer` — pinned to bottom via flex (`margin-top: auto`)

When adding pages, match `index.html` / `legal.html` (UIkit + `custom.css`).

## Content Model

Three persona cards on the homepage:

1. **Developer** — base-station.io, GitHub, LinkedIn
2. **Traveller** — Instagram
3. **Blogger** — WordPress, Tumblr

Each card: image (`<picture>` WebP), title, `.card-description`, `.card-meta`, `.card-links`.

Footer on `index.html` links to `legal.html`. Legal page has anchor sections: `#terms`, `#privacy`, `#disclaimer`.

## Deployment

Push to `main`/`master`; GitHub Pages serves files from repo root. No server-side logic.
